usage: hia_native_helper_mcp_integration.py [-h] --runtime RUNTIME
                                            --runtime-source RUNTIME_SOURCE
                                            --hepta HEPTA
                                            --expected-runtime-source
                                            EXPECTED_RUNTIME_SOURCE
                                            --expected-hepta-source
                                            EXPECTED_HEPTA_SOURCE
                                            --cold-report COLD_REPORT
                                            [--native-source-bootstrap NATIVE_SOURCE_BOOTSTRAP]
                                            [--bootstrap-distribution BOOTSTRAP_DISTRIBUTION]
                                            [--expected-bootstrap-distribution EXPECTED_BOOTSTRAP_DISTRIBUTION]
                                            [--native-bootstrap NATIVE_BOOTSTRAP]
                                            [--native-toolchain NATIVE_TOOLCHAIN]
                                            [--prebuild-execution PREBUILD_EXECUTION]
                                            [--cold-execution COLD_EXECUTION]
                                            [--post-execution POST_EXECUTION]
                                            [--release-execution RELEASE_EXECUTION]
                                            [--native-release-package NATIVE_RELEASE_PACKAGE]
                                            [--native-release-receipt NATIVE_RELEASE_RECEIPT]
                                            --output OUTPUT
                                            [--allow-disposable-sshd]

Qualify a fixed Runtime/Hepta candidate through real stdio MCP and loopback
SSH. This is an explicitly disposable GitHub-hosted-runner integration. The
worker journal and JSON adapter remain hosted Python; the scalar identity
helper and emitted workload images execute actual HIA machine code. It does
not establish production deployment, unfamiliar-model learning, or net
optimization benefit.

options:
